<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93571" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείριος</span></b> , ὁ, name of
		the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dog-star, Sirius</i>,
			whose visible heliacal rising marked the season of greatest heat
			(cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				17.39
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				587
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				609
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sc.</u>
				153
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				397
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1104
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σείριος κύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					967
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				803
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σείριος ἀστήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					417
				</span></i>
			:—of the <i>sun</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				61
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτὶς Σειρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					397
				</span></i>
			 and Sch. ad loc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἠέλιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					120
				</span></i>
			; of <i>stars</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ibyc.
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				23.62
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				779.8
			</span></i> cod. <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
			</span></i>, of a bright <i>planet</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IA</u>
				7
			</span></i> (acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Theo Sm.
				p.146
			</span></i> H., dub., anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Adj.
			<i>destructive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείριαι νᾶες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tim.
					<u>Pers.</u>
				</span></i>
			
			
			<i><span class="en">
				192
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείριον πάθος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρίασις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.124
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείριον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάτιον</span>), a <i>light summer garment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείρινα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρῆνα</span>
			. (<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> derives it from a form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείρ</span></b>  gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρός,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥλιος</span>
			, which is suspect.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
